From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: PS5: the rest of a view's last host page is free.

A view that ends inside a 16 KiB host page (an image whose size is not a multiple of 16 KiB) has the rest of that host
page mapped with it. VirtualQuery just past the view asked the native query (__wine_ps5_vm_gap), found it taken and
reported it reserved (AllocationBase that address, MEM_PRIVATE), where Windows reports MEM_FREE: kernel32 loader.c:942-946,
14 images, 4 checks, both builds, 112 lines (docs/HOST_PAGES.md, group A). Nothing can be allocated there on Windows
either, as it lies below the next 64 KiB boundary, so the space up to the end of that host page is now reported free.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index b9b0a31..7db630a 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -7570,6 +7570,17 @@ static struct file_view *get_memory_region_size( char *base, char **region_start
         void *start, *end;
         int status;
 
+        /* The rest of the last host page of a view that ends inside one (an image's tail) is mapped with the view, so the
+         * native query below finds it taken and called it reserved; Windows calls it free, and nothing can be allocated
+         * there on Windows either: it lies below the next 64 KiB boundary (kernel32 loader.c:942-946, 112 lines). */
+        if (*region_start && ((UINT_PTR)*region_start & host_page_mask) &&
+            base < (char *)ROUND_ADDR( *region_start, host_page_mask ) + host_page_size)
+        {
+            char *host_end = (char *)ROUND_ADDR( *region_start, host_page_mask ) + host_page_size;
+            if (host_end < *region_end) *region_end = host_end;
+            return NULL;
+        }
+
         /* Fixed allocations already reject this range. Do not advertise it
          * as free to Windows address-space scanners. Existing views above
          * the measured host limit were handled by the tree lookup first. */
